[al:新概念英语（二）]
[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Food and Talk]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:09.79]Was Mrs. Rumbold a good companion at dinner? | 鲁姆索尔德太太是位好的晚餐 companions 吗？
[00:15.06]Last week at a dinner party, | 在上周的一次宴会上，
[00:17.55]the hostess asked me to sit next to Mrs. Rumbold. | 女主人要我坐在鲁姆索尔德太太旁边。
[00:22.74]Mrs. Rumbold was a large, | 鲁姆索尔德太太是一位
[00:24.99]unsmiling lady in a tight black dress. | 身材高大、表情严肃、穿紧身黑连衣裙的女士。
[00:29.34]She did not even look up when I took my seat beside her. | 当我在她身旁坐下时，她连头都没抬一下。
[00:34.73]Her eyes were fixed on her plate and in a short time, | 她的双眼盯着自己的盘子，不一会儿，
[00:39.22]she was busy eating. | 就忙着吃起来了。
[00:42.09]I tried to make conversation. | 我试图找个话题和她聊聊。
[00:44.95]'A new play is coming to "The Globe" soon,' | “一出新戏就要在‘环球剧场’上演了，”
[00:48.27]I said. 'Will you be seeing it?' | 我说，“您去看吗？”
[00:53.12]'No,' she answered. | “不去，”她回答说。
[00:55.95]'Will you be spending your holidays abroad this year?' I asked. | “您今年打算在国外度假吗？”我问。
[01:03.23]'No,' she answered. | “不去，”她回答说。
[01:05.81]'Will you be staying in England?' I asked. | “您就准备待在英国吗？”我问。
[01:09.92]'No,' she answered. | “不去，”她回答说。
[01:12.94]In despair, I asked her whether she was enjoying her dinner. | 失望之中我问她饭吃得是否满意。
[01:18.50]'Young man,' she answered, | “年轻人，”她回答说，
[01:21.70]'if you ate more and talked less, we would both enjoy our dinner!' | “如果你多吃点，少说点，我们两个都会吃得满意的！”
